title: Interaction4
---
<<set $wordCount = 88>>
You are slouching again. 
I told you, 
I want you to have more pride in your appearance. 
How will the other kids at your school 
know you’re serious if you look like a slob? 
You’re a very smart kid. 
Always so respectful.
I just want other people to be able to see that. 
You know, your father and I are very proud of you. 
We always wanted you to go to a good school. 
When you got into college, 
we knew you would have opportunities we never had.
===

title: Interaction5a
---
<<set $wordCount = 14>>
It was just an observation. 
You need to lighten up. 
You’re always so dramatic.
===

title: Interaction5b
---
<<set $wordCount = 25>>
We were so worried. 
All we want is for you to have a life better than we did. 
Everything we do, we do for you.
===

title: Interaction5c
---
<<set $wordCount = 20>>
Alright. 
I guess you called me here for a reason. 
Always so dramatic. 
What did you want to speak about?
===

title: Interaction6a
---
<<set $wordCount = 75>>
Is there something the matter with you today? 
After you hadn’t bothered to answer my calls all week, 
I was excited to meet my daughter for a nice lunch. 
If you remember, you reached out to me. 
And here you are getting worked up 
after being cold and unresponsive this whole conversation. 
I swear ever since you were a child, 
everything has to be an event with you. 
I bet it’s those friends of yours.
===

title: Interaction6b
---
<<set $wordCount = 44>>
We were so worried. 
We love you very much. 
I hope you know that. 
Everyday we feel so blessed to have such a perfect daughter. 
And of course it doesn’t hurt 
that I get to brag about you to the girls at the salon.
===

title: Interaction6c
---
<<set $wordCount = 9>>
You what? 
You dropped out? 
When did this happen?
===

title: Interaction7a
---
<<set $wordCount = 48>>
I wish your father could hear the way you talk to me! 
I’m sorry, but after all that I’ve done for you, 
I don’t deserve to be treated like this. 
Everything I’ve done, I’ve done for you. 
But since I’m such a terrible mother, 
I’ll leave you alone.
===

title: Interaction7b
---
<<set $wordCount = 56>>
Now where is that waiter? 
I put in our meals well over 15 minutes ago. 
It seems good service is ridiculously hard to find these days. 
You would think they could at least come over 
and take your drink order.
Honestly!
Honey, I love you, but next time we go out, 
I am picking the restaurant.
===

title: Interaction7c
---
<<set $wordCount = 65>>
Oh no, Honey. 
You don’t have to apologize. 
And please don’t cry. 
I know, I know we put these expectations on you, 
we just want the best for you and if school isn’t that, 
we can help you work it out. 
Whatever is going on, I promise we’ll support you. 
Me and your father. 
It’s just school. 
Listen, come here. 
Thank you for telling me.
===